    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "thanks for this. it's a good start, but i'm a bit worried it's leaning a little too hard into the buzzwords. it feels a bit \"NGO-speak\" and might trigger that \"fake\" alarm with the board if they read it too closely. \n\ncan we try a version that's a bit more grounded? instead of just using the words, try to describe the actual scene—like how a village changes when they don't have to walk miles for water anymore, or how the kids can stay in school. i still need to hit those themes (the \"sustainable\", \"empower\", etc. stuff), but let's try to make it feel much more human and less like a list of objectives. basically, i need the \"heart\" of the story to come through more clearly.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
